\* TIER-2 CERT LEG — Mutation 1 (EnableUnservable = FALSE). EXPECT: VIOLATION.
\*
\* Designed harm: no unservable path => `PostDecisionLoss` is violated (participant loss
\* after a durable activation decision forces indefinite non-finalization). At the large
\* bounds this fired as a 23-state stuttering lasso on the v0.10.4 model (run 29222085672,
\* `verdict=GREEN`, §6). It must fire again HERE for the reduced bounds to certify.
\*
\* NO SYMMETRY (temporal property) — same reason as CertBaselineLiveness.cfg.
\*
\* @MAXMSGS@ is substituted by the tlc-cert workflow from the `cert_msgs` dispatch input.
SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTRAINT
CertConstraint

CONSTANTS
Stages = {s1, s2}
MaxEpoch = 1
MaxRId = 1
MaxAttempt = 2
MaxPos = 1
MaxCrashes = 1
MaxCkpt = 2
MaxMsgs = @MAXMSGS@
EnableUnservable = FALSE
ResetTruncates = TRUE
AttemptFencing = TRUE
AbortGuardEnabled = TRUE

INVARIANTS
Inv

PROPERTIES
PostDecisionLoss
